{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028571-2e-bygones","id":1028571,"title":"[2E] Bygones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T09:01:28-08:00","id":1028571,"title":"[2E] Bygones","content":"There are unique magical items described in <b>God Machine Rules Update</b> ( but <i>not</i> in <b>CoD Rulebook</b> ) called Bygones. Basically, they are Relics from 1E <b>Reliquary</b>. But here is my question:<br /> <br /> <b>How characters can understand Effect of the item?</b> <b>How they should know that Bygone is 'magical' in the first place? </b>Because 'working it out' seems counter intuitive and gameplay time waste. Question is both for the mortals testing Bygones but also for supernaturals - mages especially.<br /> <br /> If you got ideas for new Bygones, treat yourself here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-08-2017, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:25:14-08:00","id":1028582,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;working it out&quot;. And each Bygone is unique, it's not like they all have the same kind of aura you can just identify. What's wrong with a Research roll?<br /> <br /> Amechra came up with a Bygone called the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/271329-bygone-the-vitachorigisy-engine\"><b>Vitachorigisy Engine</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:16:21-08:00","id":1028642,"title":"","content":"I have a simple mortal problem - <b>How can moral know that everday item is truly magical?</b> We have room full of stuff - <b>How to point what should I take as 'special' items?</b><br /> <br /> I suppose that mages just see that item have some dense Arcana Pattern or weird Symbols hanging over it in Mage Sight. Mortals sounds as working blind there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028571-2e-bygones?p=1028582#post1028582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;working it out&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's assume our mortal know that item is 'special' somehow - <b>What, he spends all day long doing anything that comes to his mind about Bygone?</b> Sleep with it, bath with it, anything?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028571-2e-bygones?p=1028582#post1028582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And each Bygone is unique, it's not like they all have the same kind of aura you can just identify. What's wrong with a Research roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's assume Research route - <b>I suppose character is rolling Intelligence + Academics or Occult - But how many Success are needed per Bygone? Maybe something like 5 * Structure? What time intervals between rolls?</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T20:13:24-08:00","id":1028848,"title":"","content":"1- The items won't typically give any clue by themselves. A &quot;magical&quot; item will usually be found in a context that makes it stand out, like the only jewel in the corpse that wasn't robbed. Sometimes the item will be completely inconspicuous, and probably a character will get a hold of it for its mundane properties without suspecting any strange property until noticing weird phenomena around it, like if the item is the gun the character have at hand.<br /> <br /> 2- If the character suspect something and want to know details, probably research is indeed the better route. But the ST should simply choose the best way to deal with it. If you just want to give a magic item to the players and see how they choose to use it, just a single success on the roll should be enough. If you want to explore how some of those items distinguish among themselves with some being less known than others, you can make for extended rolls and choose what you think as appropriate target numbers. If you want to make the research into a story by itself, make each roll lead to a new scene, set of decisions or consequences, be creative. If you want to explore the existence of incomplete and incorrect legends about the object out there, you could make each success bring to light a couple of accounts, mixing true and false statements about it, Exceptional success should eliminate some or all false accounts, and Dramatic failures eliminate some or all true ones.<br /> <br /> 3- Otherwise, this is the kind of question you find your own answer. It isn't supposed to be an automatic perception, but it doesn't make all that difference without context. Your chronicle is the only context that can justify rule X or Y. A pedestal or uncommon box, with a instruction booklet lying around are all you need to deal quickly with it without much problem. And it isn't all that strange, for a previous user to guard it well and take note of its properties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T23:44:43-08:00","id":1028899,"title":"","content":"Why isn't the answer obvious? They lean how to use the Bygone when the Angel visits them in their dreams and reveals their glorious hidden destiny. (...as the fuel for an elaborate Occult Matrix of course! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, couldn't resist. I think research is the best option. Could lead to some good plot hooks or points involving ancient records of the Bygone or first hand accounts of people interacting with it. Or Angels, you can never go wrong with God Machine Angels. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. As for Mages, I think Mage Sight is the best solution. Just remember to use a higher Opacity because it isn't a Supernal Relic. Although you could also use Supernal Angels! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> *sprays water* (Yipe!) *bad Dusksage*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish...and bad jokes 01-09-2017, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T00:15:49-08:00","id":1028910,"title":"","content":"<b>Duskage</b>, may use Angels Visitation idea in my games, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, I think that Mysterium would rather use Mage Sight with Research solution for cataloging those various items for Atheneum. <br /> <br /> I asked similar questions to <b>Reighnhell</b> about his Relics and Bygones similarities. He has very interesting easy solution to Researching items origins, using Ephemeral Entity's as schema. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes?p=1028756#post1028756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Bygones</b><br /> The Bygone rules are interesting. They were introduced well after I started writing up Relics (primarily using rules from Reliquary with an ample amount of home-brewed adjustment). Ultimately, they are meant to represent the same types of items; objects of mysterious origin with strange abilities. Bygones are essentially Relics that aren't described in terms of Dots per Effect and they are used more as events/encounters than items to be acquired (although the line between those distinctions is blurry).<br /> <br /> As far as discovering the history and abilities of a Item (hopefully before you gouge out an eye), treat it like researching an Ephemeral Entity (<i>CofD, pg.139</i>), using the items dot rating in place of Rank. Since Bygones do not have a dot Rating, I would default to a effective Rating of 3 - adjust the number of required successes up or down depending on how challenging you want to make the research ( Mikes smokes might reduce the target number by two while Abella\u2019s Mirror might increase the target number by 4).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}